{{#if responsesAsCode}}
## Responses as code

Each turn, your entire response is run as one TypeScript program. Reply with code
alone: no prose, no Markdown, no code fences.

Your program runs synchronously — every function returns its value directly, so do
not use `await` or treat a return value as a promise. Use `console.log()` to print
anything you want to see on the next turn; a returned value is discarded. The turn
ends when your program does, and its output is given back to you.

The run continues until you call `harness.finish(summary)`. Nothing else ends it.

### Your APIs

Your program is given these objects:

{{#each apis}}
